---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Investigative Research Support for Law Enforcement | Silver Lining of Hope"
  description="Free investigative research support for detectives, agencies, and prosecutors: organized case files, records compilation, and cross-referenced missing person data."
  heading="For law enforcement"
  intro="Your caseload is impossible. Our research is free. Let us do the compiling, cleaning, and cross-referencing."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Get help', href: '/get-help' },
    { label: 'For law enforcement', href: '/get-help/law-enforcement' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="container--narrow section prose">
    <p>
      Silver Lining of Hope was built by someone who did the unglamorous part
      of investigation — records, timelines, data reconciliation — for seven
      months straight, and saw it help reopen a case. We offer that same
      disciplined support to detectives, sheriffs' offices, state police, and
      prosecutors, at no cost, with no interference in your investigation and
      no public commentary about your agency.
    </p>

    <h2>What we can take off your desk</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Case file organization</strong> — converting a family's box
        of documents, screenshots, and memories into a clean, chronological,
        indexed file.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Open-source and database research</strong> — compiling and
        reconciling entries across NamUs, the Doe Network, the Charley
        Project, and public records, and flagging discrepancies worth a
        second look.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Missing person data for your district</strong> — through
        <a href="/programs/the-missing-link">The Missing Link</a>, we're
        building cleaned, cross-referenced data on 1,000+ Indiana missing
        person cases, organized by Indiana State Police district.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Family liaison support</strong> — a trained advocate who
        keeps families informed and prepared, which means fewer difficult
        calls to your desk and better cooperation when you need it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we operate</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We work through proper channels and follow your agency's lead on active cases.</li>
      <li>We don't name suspects, run public theories, or feed media speculation.</li>
      <li>We document sources for everything we hand you.</li>
      <li>We're a 501(c)(3) (EIN 39-2169099) — there is never a fee or a fundraising condition attached to case support.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Start a conversation</h2>
    <p>
      Whether it's one cold case, a district's worth of missing person
      records, or a family that needs a steady liaison,
      <a href="/about/contact">contact us</a> and we'll scope it together.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
